# OpenStack DevStack Lab

This project demonstrates the installation and configuration of an OpenStack environment using DevStack in a virtualized setup.

# Overview
The goal of this project is to deploy a functional OpenStack cloud environment on limited hardware resources and understand the IaaS architecture.

# Environment
- Host OS: Windows 10
- Virtualization: Oracle VirtualBox
- Guest OS: Ubuntu Server 22.04 LTS
- RAM: 16GB (allocated to VM)
- Storage: 70GB
- Networking: NAT with Port Forwarding

# OpenStack Setup
- Installed using DevStack (single-node / all-in-one)
- Core services:
  - Nova (Compute)
  - Neutron (Networking)
  - Glance (Images)
  - Keystone (Authentication)
  - Horizon (Dashboard)

# Networking
- NAT configuration due to hardware limitations
- Port Forwarding:
  - SSH → 2222
  - HTTP (Horizon) → 8080
- Access via: http://localhost:8080/dashboard

# Instances
- Created test instances using Cirros image
- Verified functionality using:
- Horizon Dashboard
- CLI (`virsh list --all`, console access)

# Limitations
- Single-node architecture (DevStack)
- No High Availability
- Limited networking access (NAT environment)
- Not suitable for production use

# Future Improvements
- Multi-node OpenStack deployment
- Integration with Ansible / Kolla-Ansible
- Use of external networking and floating IPs
- Container workloads (Docker / Kubernetes)

# Additional Project (Monitoring Stack)

An additional cloud-based setup was implemented inside an OpenStack instance:

- Node-RED for data ingestion
- InfluxDB for time-series data storage
- Grafana for data visualization

This setup demonstrates how OpenStack instances can host real-world applications and monitoring systems.

